            "review_text": "Jagsta\nIsle of Man, United Kingdom31 contributions\n0\nSadly let down by its vibe.\nFeb 2024 • Couples\nWhat a shame. This bar/restaurant is in the middle of the Sunset Town night market. It offers some great quality small plates and larger meals and a great range of drinks, but is let down by its ambience. Choose your target demographic, and choose an appropriate vibe for them. This is a bar in the midst of a family orientated night market. The style of food and range of cocktails suggests that a chilled \"cocktail lounge\" vibe would be appropriate. The resident DJ chose his vibe- some fairly hardcore rap, at a volume that prevented normal conversation. \nThe second night we went there was a European girl there who seemed to be managing the place. She said there'd been complaints about the music and shed chosen a perfect chilled vibe. \nThe night after she wasn't there. Back to rap. We left. \nCould merit 4 or 5 stars for food and drinks. \nIt also seems that the volume and choice of music will also impact those establishments adjacent to Gion.\nRead more\nWritten February 13, 2024",
